      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define customer guidance prompts and service scripts for key categories.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 427273,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Okay team, following up on our pain points. I've cleaned up the Customer Questions Log (A1) with everyone's input. Now we need to tackle T2: drafting guidance prompts for our top 5 categories. Let's start with Electronics and Denim. What are some good opening questions we can use?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 177366,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "For electronics, maybe something like 'Are you looking for something for work, for home, or for fun?' to help narrow it down.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 486724,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "For denim, I usually ask 'What kind of fit are you looking for?'. Like slim, relaxed, straight. It's a good starting point.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 244639,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "i just ask 'can i help you find anything'.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 246501,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "That's a classic, but we want to try more open questions to get them talking. The suggestions from @177366 and @486724 are great. Let's build on those. I've started a doc for this, A2. I'll add these and we can build it out for all 5 categories.",
            "mentions": [
              177366,
              486724
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 427273,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "I've just added a few more examples to A2 for the other categories. Also included some product recommendation phrases, like 'If you like X, you might also want to check out Y'.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 486724,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "This is looking good. Just a thought - we should make sure these prompts don't conflict with our returns policy. For example, we shouldn't promise something will 'last forever'. I can cross-check with the official policy docs and also our work on T5.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "shield",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 246501,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "Excellent point, @486724. Safety first. Please do that check. In the meantime, I've consolidated the suggestions in A2 into a clean first version. Can everyone take a look and give a thumbs up if you're happy for this to be our V1 to test out?",
